{"name":"Hot Chocolate","hex":"#683939","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hot chocolate","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A warm beverage usually made of cocoa and water or milk.","A powder usually made from cocoa used to prepare this beverage."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To consume hot  chocolate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hot_chocolate"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hot Chocolate","blocks":[{"text":"Hot Chocolate are a British soul band formed by Errol Brown and Tony Wilson. The group had at least one hit song every year on the UK Singles Chart from 1970 to 1984."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/The_Hot_Chocolate.jpg/330px-The_Hot_Chocolate.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hot_Chocolate","wikidata":"Q1368881"},{"title":"Hot chocolate","blocks":[{"text":"Hot chocolate, also known as hot cocoa or drinking chocolate, is a heated drink consisting of shaved or melted chocolate or cocoa powder, and heated milk or water. It usually contains a sweetener, such as sugar, and is often garnished with whipped cream or marshmallows. Hot chocolate made with melted chocolate is characterized by less sweetness and a thicker consistency."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/After_The_St._Patrick%27s_Parade_Late_Lunch_%40_Lemon%2C_Dawson_Street%2C_Dublin%2C_Rep._Of_Ireland_A_Fine_Tradition%21_%286992614913%29.jpg/330px-After_The_St._Patrick%27s_Parade_Late_Lunch_%40_Lemon%2C_Dawson_Street%2C_Dublin%2C_Rep._Of_Ireland_A_Fine_Tradition%21_%286992614913%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hot_chocolate","wikidata":"Q13261"},{"title":"Chocolate","blocks":[{"text":"Chocolate is a food made from roasted and ground cocoa beans. It can be a liquid, solid, or paste. It is eaten on its own and used to flavor other foods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Three_Bars_%281%29.jpg/330px-Three_Bars_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chocolate","wikidata":"Q195"},{"title":"Chocolate (color)","blocks":[{"text":"The color chocolate or cocoa brown is a shade of brown that resembles chocolate. At right is displayed the color traditionally called chocolate."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Chocolate02.jpg/330px-Chocolate02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chocolate_(color)","wikidata":"Q3309916"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/1998_hot_chocolate_cologne.jpg/500px-1998_hot_chocolate_cologne.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/1998_hot_chocolate_cologne.jpg/1280px-1998_hot_chocolate_cologne.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/1998_hot_chocolate_cologne.jpg/500px-1998_hot_chocolate_cologne.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Errol Brown performing on stage in 1998","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1998_hot_chocolate_cologne.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Chocolatepot.jpg/250px-Chocolatepot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8d/Chocolatepot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Chocolatepot.jpg/250px-Chocolatepot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Silver chocolate pot, Fr